.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt MDC2_INIT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm MDC2 ,
.Nm MDC2_Init ,
.Nm MDC2_Update ,
.Nm MDC2_Final
.Nd MDC2 hash function
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/mdc2.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft unsigned char *
.Fo MDC2
.Fa "const unsigned char *d"
.Fa "unsigned long n"
.Fa "unsigned char *md"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo MDC2_Init
.Fa "MDC2_CTX *c"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo MDC2_Update
.Fa "MDC2_CTX *c"
.Fa "const unsigned char *data"
.Fa "unsigned long len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo MDC2_Final
.Fa "unsigned char *md"
.Fa "MDC2_CTX *c"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_DigestInit_ex 3 ,
.Xr EVP_DigestUpdate 3
and
.Xr EVP_DigestFinal_ex 3 .
.Pp
MDC2 is a method to construct hash functions with 128 bit output from
block ciphers.
These functions are an implementation of MDC2 with DES.
.Pp
.Fn MDC2
computes the MDC2 message digest of the
.Fa n
bytes at
.Fa d
and places it in
.Fa md
(which must have space for MDC2_DIGEST_LENGTH == 16 bytes of output).
If
.Fa md
is NULL, the digest is placed in a static array.
.Pp
The following functions may be used if the message is not completely
stored in memory:
.Pp
.Fn MDC2_Init
initializes a
.Vt MDC2_CTX
structure.
.Pp
.Fn MDC2_Update
can be called repeatedly with chunks of the message to be hashed
.Pf ( Fa len
bytes at
.Fa data Ns ).
.Pp
.Fn MDC2_Final
places the message digest in
.Fa md ,
which must have space for MDC2_DIGEST_LENGTH == 16 bytes of output, and
erases the
.Vt MDC2_CTX .
.Pp
Applications should use the higher level functions
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
etc.
instead of calling the hash functions directly.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn MDC2
returns a pointer to the hash value.
.Pp
.Fn MDC2_Init ,
.Fn MDC2_Update
and
.Fn MDC2_Final
return 1 for success, 0 otherwise.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
ISO/IEC 10118-2:2000 Hash-Function 2, with DES as the underlying block
cipher.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
